1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,909
This channel was built by an artificial
intelligence.

2
00:00:02,929 --> 00:00:06,434
The name, the logo, the banner, the
editing tools.

3
00:00:06,454 --> 00:00:07,181
Everything.

4
00:00:07,201 --> 00:00:09,193
All I typed were my passwords.

5
00:00:09,213 --> 00:00:13,989
And I'll show you everything: the methods,
the failures, the views, and the money.

6
00:00:14,009 --> 00:00:15,540
This is day one.

7
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:19,669
At noon, I gave Claude, Anthropic's AI, a
single instruction.

8
00:00:19,689 --> 00:00:23,326
Build a news channel, in French and
English, and publish everything

9
00:00:23,346 --> 00:00:24,090
automatically.

10
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:26,948
Within minutes, it had a full visual
identity.

11
00:00:26,968 --> 00:00:31,601
Then it opened a GitHub repository and
wrote six video editing programs on its

12
00:00:31,621 --> 00:00:31,840
own.

13
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:34,186
First obstacle: the name.

14
00:00:34,206 --> 00:00:35,695
Tempo News, taken.

15
00:00:35,715 --> 00:00:37,241
Tempo Daily, taken.

16
00:00:37,261 --> 00:00:38,228
Daily Brief, taken too.

17
00:00:38,248 --> 00:00:39,886
Nine handles rejected.

18
00:00:39,906 --> 00:00:42,149
Only one was free: Tempo Brief.

19
00:00:42,169 --> 00:00:43,580
The channel existed.

20
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:46,019
Next, it checked Google Trends and picked
a topic.

21
00:00:46,039 --> 00:00:47,735
Anthropic going public.

22
00:00:47,755 --> 00:00:49,030
Its own creator.

23
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:52,830
It edited the video, but with drone shots
of New York that had nothing to do with

24
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:53,299
the story.

25
00:00:53,319 --> 00:00:55,480
And in the voiceover, there was this.

26
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:01,786
“Read this as a TV news anchor, deep,
calm, articulate, brisk but natural pace,

27
00:01:01,806 --> 00:01:04,580
no excessive emphasis.” (in French)

28
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:07,451
The voice was reading its instructions out
loud.

29
00:01:07,471 --> 00:01:08,463
I said no.

30
00:01:08,483 --> 00:01:09,714
Nothing was published.

31
00:01:09,734 --> 00:01:12,950
New rule: I approve every topic before
production.

32
00:01:12,970 --> 00:01:14,675
And a real problem showed up.

33
00:01:14,695 --> 00:01:19,088
For sports, movies or celebrities, there
is almost no copyright-free footage.

34
00:01:19,108 --> 00:01:20,592
So we changed course.

35
00:01:20,612 --> 00:01:22,723
The channel is now called Brief A I.

36
00:01:22,743 --> 00:01:26,080
And it covers what it knows best:
artificial intelligence.

37
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:31,029
Day one: three and a half hours, a
complete channel, six programs, one

38
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:33,716
rejected video, and zero views so far.

39
00:01:33,736 --> 00:01:35,866
AI is fast at execution.

40
00:01:35,886 --> 00:01:39,120
But deciding what is worth making is still
a human job.

41
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:44,580
From now on, every week, I'll publish the
real numbers: views, subscribers, costs

42
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:45,389
and revenue.

43
00:01:45,409 --> 00:01:47,460
Subscribe to follow the experiment.
